  "goodToKnow": "Der Rosenmontag is Carnival Monday, the Monday before Aschermittwoch (Ash Wednesday) and the climax of Karneval in the Rhineland. Huge Rosenmontagszüge with satirical floats roll through Cologne, Düsseldorf and Mainz, throwing sweets (Kamelle) to crowds shouting Alaaf or Helau. Many offices close in these cities. The name probably comes from dialect rosen (to rave), not roses. Plural: die Rosenmontage."
